/-!
# Maximal subgroups of infinite index in branch groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 15.15)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 15.15 (L. Bartholdi, R. I. Grigorchuk, Z.
Šunić): is every maximal subgroup of a finitely generated branch group necessarily of finite index?

This module defines the branch group formulation of Kourovka Problem 15.15 and proves
Bondarenko's counterexample.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 15.15 (L.
Bartholdi, R. I. Grigorchuk, Z. Šunić). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701103 (`KOU-15.15`), dataset
ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Branch groups follow Problem 15.12: a faithful, level-transitive action by automorphisms on a rooted
tree in which every rigid level stabilizer (the subgroup generated by the rigid vertex stabilizers
of the vertices of one level, a rigid vertex stabilizer consisting of the elements whose support
lies in the subtree below the vertex) has finite index. Level-transitivity forces the tree to be
spherically homogeneous, so the tree is modelled as the words whose `i`-th letter is below `m i`,
with all branching indices `m i ≥ 2` as in Grigorchuk's setting (the survey cited in 15.12); tree
automorphisms are the permutations of the vertices preserving the prefix (ancestor) order in both
directions. This is the geometric definition of L. Bartholdi, R. I. Grigorchuk and Z. Šunić, Branch
groups, Handbook of Algebra 3 (2003), arXiv:math/0510294 (Definition 1.13, on the trees of words
with all `m i ≥ 2` of Section 1.2), which their open-problems chapter uses for its versions of
Problems 15.14 (b), (c), 15.15, 15.17 and 15.18 (Questions 20, 15, 14, 10, 9 and 11); Kionke and
Schesler (Section 2.1) and Bondarenko (Section 2) use the same definition. A maximal subgroup is a
coatom of the subgroup lattice (`IsCoatom`).

The example uses the alternating group on five letters both at the root and in a directed
copy whose nontrivial vertex permutations lie along subtrees branching off a fixed ray.
Every subtree supports a copy of the example group. The images of the copies on an infinite
family of disjoint subtrees must repeat in any finite quotient. Commutation and perfectness
then force a level stabilizer into the kernel. The proper subgroup of finitary elements
agrees with the whole group on every level, so any maximal subgroup containing it has
infinite index.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.BranchGroupInfiniteIndexMaximalKourovka15Problem15Wanted

/-- **Vertices of the spherically homogeneous rooted tree (Kourovka 15.15).** For a branching
sequence $m \colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$, the vertices of the spherically homogeneous rooted
tree are the finite words $(x_0, \dots, x_{k-1})$ of natural numbers with $x_i < m(i)$ for every
$i < k$. The length $k$ of a word is its level and its prefixes are its ancestors. -/
def TreeVertex (m : ℕ → ℕ) : Type :=
  {l : List ℕ // ∀ (i : ℕ) (h : i < l.length), l[i] < m i}

/-- **Rigid vertex stabilizer (Kourovka 15.15).** Let $\rho$ be a homomorphism from a group $G$ to
the permutations of the vertices of the tree with branching sequence $m$, and let $v$ be a vertex.
The rigid vertex stabilizer of $v$ is the set of $g \in G$ such that $\rho(g)$ fixes every vertex
$w$ of which $v$ is not a prefix, that is, every vertex outside the subtree rooted at $v$. -/
def rigidVertexStabilizer {m : ℕ → ℕ} {G : Type*} [Group G] (ρ : G →* Equiv.Perm (TreeVertex m))
    (v : TreeVertex m) : Set G :=
  {g | ∀ w : TreeVertex m, ¬ v.1 <+: w.1 → ρ g w = w}

/-- **Rigid level stabilizer (Kourovka 15.15).** Let $\rho$ be a homomorphism from a group $G$ to
the permutations of the vertices of the tree with branching sequence $m$, and let $n$ be a natural
number. The $n$-th rigid level stabilizer is the subgroup of $G$ generated by the rigid vertex
stabilizers of all vertices at level $n$. -/
def rigidLevelStabilizer {m : ℕ → ℕ} {G : Type*} [Group G] (ρ : G →* Equiv.Perm (TreeVertex m))
    (n : ℕ) : Subgroup G :=
  Subgroup.closure (⋃ v ∈ {v : TreeVertex m | v.1.length = n}, rigidVertexStabilizer ρ v)

/-- **Branch group (Kourovka 15.15).** A group $G$ is a branch group if there are a sequence
$m \colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ with $m(i) \ge 2$ for all $i$ and an injective homomorphism
$\rho$ from $G$ to the permutations of the vertices of the spherically homogeneous rooted tree with
branching sequence $m$ such that each $\rho(g)$ is a tree automorphism (for all vertices $v$ and
$w$, $v$ is a prefix of $w$ if and only if $\rho(g)(v)$ is a prefix of $\rho(g)(w)$), the action is
level-transitive (for any two vertices $v$ and $w$ at the same level some $g \in G$ has
$\rho(g)(v) = w$), and for every $n$ the $n$-th rigid level stabilizer has finite index in $G$. -/
def IsBranchGroup (G : Type*) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∃ (m : ℕ → ℕ) (_ : ∀ i, 2 ≤ m i) (ρ : G →* Equiv.Perm (TreeVertex m)),
    Function.Injective ρ ∧
    (∀ (g : G) (v w : TreeVertex m), v.1 <+: w.1 ↔ (ρ g v).1 <+: (ρ g w).1) ∧
    (∀ v w : TreeVertex m, v.1.length = w.1.length → ∃ g : G, ρ g v = w) ∧
    ∀ n : ℕ, (rigidLevelStabilizer ρ n).FiniteIndex

/-- **Kourovka 15.15: maximal subgroups of finitely generated branch groups have finite index.**
The statement (L. Bartholdi, R. I. Grigorchuk, Z. Šunić) that every maximal subgroup of every
finitely generated branch group has finite index. -/
def branchGroupMaximalSubgroupsFiniteIndex : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], Group.FG G → IsBranchGroup G →
    ∀ M : Subgroup G, IsCoatom M → M.FiniteIndex

open Equiv Equiv.Perm
open scoped commutatorElement

local notation "X" => Fin 5
local notation "W" => List X
local notation "P" => Equiv.Perm W
local notation "A" => alternatingGroup X

private instance aPerfect : Group.IsPerfect A :=
  ⟨commutator_alternatingGroup_eq_top (by simp)⟩

private def nodeFun (s : Equiv.Perm X) (f : X → P) : W → W
  | [] => []
  | x :: w => s x :: f x w

private def node (s : Equiv.Perm X) (f : X → P) : P where
  toFun := nodeFun s f
  invFun := nodeFun s⁻¹ (fun x => (f (s⁻¹ x))⁻¹)
  left_inv := by
    rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩) <;> simp [nodeFun]
  right_inv := by
    rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩) <;> simp [nodeFun]

@[simp] private theorem node_nil (s : Equiv.Perm X) (f : X → P) : node s f [] = [] := rfl

@[simp] private theorem node_cons (s : Equiv.Perm X) (f : X → P) (x : X) (w : W) :
    node s f (x :: w) = s x :: f x w := rfl

@[simp] private theorem node_one : node 1 (fun _ => 1) = 1 := by
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩) <;> simp

private theorem node_mul (s t : Equiv.Perm X) (f h : X → P) :
    node s f * node t h = node (s * t) (fun x => f (t x) * h x) := by
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩) <;> simp [Perm.mul_apply]

private theorem node_inv (s : Equiv.Perm X) (f : X → P) :
    (node s f)⁻¹ = node s⁻¹ (fun x => (f (s⁻¹ x))⁻¹) := by
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩) <;> rfl

private def root : A →* P where
  toFun a := node a.1 (fun _ => 1)
  map_one' := node_one
  map_mul' a b := by simp [node_mul]

@[simp] private theorem root_nil (a : A) : root a [] = [] := rfl

@[simp] private theorem root_cons (a : A) (x : X) (w : W) :
    root a (x :: w) = a.1 x :: w := rfl

private def localize (x : X) : P →* P where
  toFun g := node 1 (fun y => if x = y then g else 1)
  map_one' := by simp
  map_mul' g h := by
    rw [node_mul]
    simp only [mul_one, Perm.one_apply]
    congr 1
    funext y
    split <;> simp_all

@[simp] private theorem localize_nil (x : X) (g : P) : localize x g [] = [] := rfl

@[simp] private theorem localize_cons (x y : X) (g : P) (w : W) :
    localize x g (y :: w) = y :: (if x = y then g w else w) := by
  change y :: (if x = y then g else 1) w = _
  split <;> rfl

private def directedFun (a : A) : W → W
  | [] => []
  | x :: w => x :: (if x = 0 then directedFun a w else if x = 1 then root a w else w)

private theorem directedFun_one (w : W) : directedFun 1 w = w := by
  induction w with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons x w ih => simp [directedFun, ih]

private theorem directedFun_mul (a b : A) (w : W) :
    directedFun (a * b) w = directedFun a (directedFun b w) := by
  induction w with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons x w ih =>
    simp only [directedFun, List.cons.injEq, true_and]
    split
    · simp [ih]
    · split <;> simp

private def directedPerm (a : A) : P where
  toFun := directedFun a
  invFun := directedFun a⁻¹
  left_inv w := by rw [← directedFun_mul, inv_mul_cancel, directedFun_one]
  right_inv w := by rw [← directedFun_mul, mul_inv_cancel, directedFun_one]

private def directed : A →* P where
  toFun := directedPerm
  map_one' := Equiv.ext directedFun_one
  map_mul' a b := Equiv.ext (directedFun_mul a b)

@[simp] private theorem directed_nil (a : A) : directed a [] = [] := rfl

@[simp] private theorem directed_cons (a : A) (x : X) (w : W) :
    directed a (x :: w) = x :: (if x = 0 then directed a w else if x = 1 then root a w else w) :=
  rfl

private theorem directed_split (a : A) :
    directed a = localize 0 (directed a) * localize 1 (root a) := by
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩)
  · simp [Perm.mul_apply]
  · by_cases h0 : x = 0
    · subst x
      simp [Perm.mul_apply]
    · by_cases h1 : x = 1
      · subst x
        simp [Perm.mul_apply]
      · simp [Perm.mul_apply, h0, h1, Ne.symm h0, Ne.symm h1]

private def exampleGroup : Subgroup P := root.range ⊔ directed.range

private theorem root_mem (a : A) : root a ∈ exampleGroup :=
  (show root.range ≤ exampleGroup from le_sup_left) (⟨a, rfl⟩)

private theorem directed_mem (a : A) : directed a ∈ exampleGroup :=
  (show directed.range ≤ exampleGroup from le_sup_right) (⟨a, rfl⟩)

private def turn : A :=
  ⟨swap 0 2 * swap 2 3, by
    rw [mem_alternatingGroup, Perm.sign_mul, Perm.sign_swap (by decide),
      Perm.sign_swap (by decide)]
    simp⟩

private theorem turn_zero : turn.1 0 = 2 := by decide

private theorem turn_one : turn.1 1 = 1 := by decide

private theorem root_conj_localize (a : A) (x : X) (g : P) :
    root a * localize x g * (root a)⁻¹ = localize (a.1 x) g := by
  have hInv : (root a)⁻¹ = root a⁻¹ := (map_inv root a).symm
  rw [hInv]
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨y, w⟩)
  · simp only [Perm.mul_apply, root_nil, localize_nil]
  · have hy : x = a.1⁻¹ y ↔ a.1 x = y := a.1.eq_symm_apply
    simp only [Perm.mul_apply, root_cons, localize_cons,
      show (a⁻¹ : A).1 = a.1⁻¹ from rfl, show a.1 (a.1⁻¹ y) = y from a.1.apply_symm_apply y, hy]

private theorem turn_directed (a : A) :
    root turn * directed a * (root turn)⁻¹ =
      localize 2 (directed a) * localize 1 (root a) := by
  calc
    _ = root turn * (localize 0 (directed a) * localize 1 (root a)) *
        (root turn)⁻¹ := congrArg (fun g => root turn * g * (root turn)⁻¹) (directed_split a)
    _ = (root turn * localize 0 (directed a) * (root turn)⁻¹) *
        (root turn * localize 1 (root a) * (root turn)⁻¹) := by group
    _ = _ := by simp [root_conj_localize, turn_zero, turn_one]

-- The two directed automorphisms overlap only in the subtree below the first-level vertex 1.
private theorem lamp_commutator (a b : A) :
    ⁅directed a, root turn * directed b * (root turn)⁻¹⁆ = localize 1 (root ⁅a, b⁆) := by
  rw [turn_directed, directed_split a]
  simp only [commutatorElement_def, mul_inv_rev, ← map_inv, map_mul]
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩)
  · simp only [Perm.mul_apply, localize_nil]
  · have hd (c : A) (u : W) : directed c (directed c⁻¹ u) = u := by
      rw [map_inv]
      exact (directed c).apply_symm_apply u
    fin_cases x <;> simp [Perm.mul_apply, -map_inv, hd]

private theorem lamp_mem (a : A) : localize 1 (root a) ∈ exampleGroup := by
  let f := (localize 1).comp root
  have hf : commutator A ≤ exampleGroup.comap f := by
    apply Subgroup.commutator_le.mpr
    intro x _ y _
    change localize 1 (root ⁅x, y⁆) ∈ exampleGroup
    rw [← lamp_commutator]
    have hu := directed_mem x
    have hv := exampleGroup.mul_mem (exampleGroup.mul_mem (root_mem turn) (directed_mem y))
      (exampleGroup.inv_mem (root_mem turn))
    exact exampleGroup.mul_mem (exampleGroup.mul_mem (exampleGroup.mul_mem hu hv)
      (exampleGroup.inv_mem hu)) (exampleGroup.inv_mem hv)
  exact hf (Group.IsPerfect.mem_commutator (g := a))

private theorem letter_transitive (x y : X) : ∃ a : A, a.1 x = y := by
  let := alternatingGroup.isPreprimitive_of_three_le_card X (by simp)
  exact MulAction.exists_smul_eq A x y

private theorem localized_root_mem (x : X) (a : A) : localize x (root a) ∈ exampleGroup := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := letter_transitive 1 x
  rw [← hb, ← root_conj_localize]
  exact exampleGroup.mul_mem (exampleGroup.mul_mem (root_mem b) (lamp_mem a))
    (exampleGroup.inv_mem (root_mem b))

private theorem localized_directed_mem (x : X) (a : A) :
    localize x (directed a) ∈ exampleGroup := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := letter_transitive 0 x
  rw [← hb, ← root_conj_localize]
  have h0 : localize 0 (directed a) ∈ exampleGroup := by
    rw [← mul_inv_cancel_right (localize 0 (directed a)) (localize 1 (root a)),
      ← directed_split a]
    exact exampleGroup.mul_mem (directed_mem a) (exampleGroup.inv_mem (lamp_mem a))
  exact exampleGroup.mul_mem (exampleGroup.mul_mem (root_mem b) h0)
    (exampleGroup.inv_mem (root_mem b))

private theorem localized_mem (x : X) (g : exampleGroup) : localize x g.1 ∈ exampleGroup := by
  have h : exampleGroup ≤ exampleGroup.comap (localize x) := sup_le
    (by rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩; exact localized_root_mem x a)
    (by rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩; exact localized_directed_mem x a)
  exact h g.2

private def rootG : A →* exampleGroup := root.codRestrict exampleGroup root_mem

private def directedG : A →* exampleGroup := directed.codRestrict exampleGroup directed_mem

private def localG (x : X) : exampleGroup →* exampleGroup :=
  ((localize x).comp exampleGroup.subtype).codRestrict exampleGroup (localized_mem x)

@[simp] private theorem local_g_val (x : X) (g : exampleGroup) :
    (localG x g).1 = localize x g.1 := rfl

local notation "Γ" => (exampleGroup : Type)

private instance exampleFG : Group.FG Γ := by
  have : Finite root.range := Finite.of_surjective _ root.rangeRestrict_surjective
  have : Finite directed.range := Finite.of_surjective _ directed.rangeRestrict_surjective
  exact (Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg _).2 <|
    ((Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg root.range).1 Monoid.fg_of_finite).sup
      ((Group.fg_iff_subgroup_fg directed.range).1 Monoid.fg_of_finite)

private theorem decompose (g : Γ) :
    ∃ (a : A) (f : X → Γ), g.1 = node a.1 (fun x => (f x).1) := by
  let K : Subgroup P :=
    { carrier := {p | ∃ (a : A) (f : X → Γ), p = node a.1 (fun x => (f x).1)}
      one_mem' := ⟨1, fun _ => 1, node_one.symm⟩
      mul_mem' := by
        rintro _ _ ⟨a, f, rfl⟩ ⟨b, h, rfl⟩
        exact ⟨a * b, fun x => f (b.1 x) * h x, node_mul _ _ _ _⟩
      inv_mem' := by
        rintro _ ⟨a, f, rfl⟩
        exact ⟨a⁻¹, fun x => (f (a.1⁻¹ x))⁻¹, node_inv _ _⟩ }
  have hK : exampleGroup ≤ K := by
    apply sup_le
    · rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨a, fun _ => 1, rfl⟩
    · rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨1, fun x => if x = 0 then directedG a else if x = 1 then rootG a else 1, ?_⟩
      apply Equiv.ext
      rintro (_ | ⟨x, w⟩)
      · rfl
      · simp only [directed_cons, node_cons, Subgroup.coe_one, Perm.one_apply]
        split <;> first | rfl | split <;> rfl
  exact hK g.2

private def sections (f : X → Γ) : Γ :=
  localG 0 (f 0) * localG 1 (f 1) * localG 2 (f 2) * localG 3 (f 3) * localG 4 (f 4)

@[simp] private theorem sections_nil (f : X → Γ) : (sections f).1 [] = [] := rfl

@[simp] private theorem sections_cons (f : X → Γ) (x : X) (w : W) :
    (sections f).1 (x :: w) = x :: (f x).1 w := by
  fin_cases x <;> rfl

private def assemble (a : A) (f : X → Γ) : Γ := rootG a * sections f

@[simp] private theorem assemble_nil (a : A) (f : X → Γ) : (assemble a f).1 [] = [] := rfl

@[simp] private theorem assemble_cons (a : A) (f : X → Γ) (x : X) (w : W) :
    (assemble a f).1 (x :: w) = a.1 x :: (f x).1 w := by
  change root a ((sections f).1 (x :: w)) = _
  simp

private theorem assemble_decompose (g : Γ) : ∃ (a : A) (f : X → Γ), g = assemble a f := by
  obtain ⟨a, f, hg⟩ := decompose g
  refine ⟨a, f, Subtype.ext (Equiv.ext fun w => ?_)⟩
  rw [hg]
  cases w <;> simp

@[simp] private theorem act_nil (g : Γ) : g.1 [] = [] := by
  obtain ⟨a, f, rfl⟩ := assemble_decompose g
  simp

@[simp] private theorem act_length (g : Γ) (w : W) : (g.1 w).length = w.length := by
  induction w generalizing g with
  | nil => simp
  | cons x w ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, f, rfl⟩ := assemble_decompose g
    simp [ih]

private theorem act_prefix (g : Γ) (v w : W) : v <+: w ↔ g.1 v <+: g.1 w := by
  induction v generalizing w g with
  | nil => simp
  | cons x v ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, f, rfl⟩ := assemble_decompose g
    cases w with
    | nil => simp
    | cons y w =>
      simp only [List.cons_prefix_cons, assemble_cons, Equiv.apply_eq_iff_eq]
      by_cases h : x = y
      · subst y
        simpa only [true_and] using ih (f x) w
      · simp [h]

private def embed : W → Γ →* Γ
  | [] => MonoidHom.id Γ
  | x :: w => (localG x).comp (embed w)

@[simp] private theorem embed_nil (g : Γ) : embed [] g = g := rfl

@[simp] private theorem embed_cons (x : X) (v : W) (g : Γ) :
    embed (x :: v) g = localG x (embed v g) := rfl

private theorem embed_fixes (v w : W) (g : Γ) (h : ¬ v <+: w) :
    (embed v g).1 w = w := by
  induction v generalizing w with
  | nil => simp at h
  | cons x v ih =>
    cases w with
    | nil => simp
    | cons y w =>
      by_cases hxy : x = y
      · subst y
        have hv : ¬ v <+: w := fun hw => h (List.cons_prefix_cons.mpr ⟨rfl, hw⟩)
        simp [ih w hv]
      · simp [hxy]

private theorem level_transitive (v w : W) (hl : v.length = w.length) :
    ∃ g : Γ, g.1 v = w := by
  induction v generalizing w with
  | nil =>
    have : w = [] := List.length_eq_zero_iff.mp hl.symm
    subst w
    exact ⟨1, rfl⟩
  | cons x v ih =>
    cases w with
    | nil => simp at hl
    | cons y w =>
      have hl' : v.length = w.length := Nat.succ.inj hl
      obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := ih w hl'
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := letter_transitive x y
      exact ⟨assemble a (fun _ => k), by simp [ha, hk]⟩

private def Level (n : ℕ) := {v : W // v.length = n}

private instance levelFinite (n : ℕ) : Finite (Level n) := by
  let f (v : Level n) (i : Fin n) : X := v.1[i.1]'(by simpa only [v.2] using i.2)
  apply Finite.of_injective f
  intro v w h
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply List.ext_getElem (v.2.trans w.2.symm)
  intro i hi _
  exact congrFun h ⟨i, by simpa only [v.2] using hi⟩

private def levelAction (n : ℕ) : Γ →* Equiv.Perm (Level n) where
  toFun g :=
    { toFun := fun w => ⟨g.1 w.1, (act_length g w.1).trans w.2⟩
      invFun := fun w => ⟨(g⁻¹ : Γ).1 w.1, (act_length g⁻¹ w.1).trans w.2⟩
      left_inv := fun w => Subtype.ext (g.1.symm_apply_apply w.1)
      right_inv := fun w => Subtype.ext (g.1.apply_symm_apply w.1) }
  map_one' := Equiv.ext fun _ => rfl
  map_mul' _ _ := Equiv.ext fun _ => rfl

private def levelCopies (n : ℕ) : Subgroup Γ :=
  ⨆ w : Level n, (embed w.1).range

private theorem localize_level_copies (n : ℕ) (x : X) {g : Γ} (hg : g ∈ levelCopies n) :
    localG x g ∈ levelCopies (n + 1) := by
  suffices levelCopies n ≤ (levelCopies (n + 1)).comap (localG x) from this hg
  apply iSup_le
  rintro w _ ⟨k, rfl⟩
  exact (le_iSup (fun v : Level (n + 1) => (embed v.1).range)
    ⟨x :: w.1, congrArg Nat.succ w.2⟩) ⟨k, rfl⟩

private theorem level_ker_le_copies (n : ℕ) :
    (levelAction n).ker ≤ levelCopies n := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro g _
    exact (le_iSup (fun v : Level 0 => (embed v.1).range) ⟨[], rfl⟩) ⟨g, rfl⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    rintro g hg
    obtain ⟨a, f, rfl⟩ := assemble_decompose g
    have hfix (x : X) (w : W) (hw : w.length = n) :
        a.1 x = x ∧ (f x).1 w = w := by
      have h := congrArg (fun p : Equiv.Perm (Level (n + 1)) =>
        (p ⟨x :: w, congrArg Nat.succ hw⟩).1) (MonoidHom.mem_ker.mp hg)
      change (assemble a f).1 (x :: w) = x :: w at h
      simpa only [assemble_cons, List.cons.injEq] using h
    have ha : a = 1 := Subtype.ext (Equiv.ext fun x =>
      (hfix x (List.replicate n 0) (by simp)).1)
    have hf (x : X) : f x ∈ (levelAction n).ker := MonoidHom.mem_ker.mpr
      (Equiv.ext fun w => Subtype.ext (hfix x w.1 w.2).2)
    rw [ha, assemble, map_one, one_mul, sections]
    exact Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.mul_mem _
      (localize_level_copies n 0 (ih (hf 0))) (localize_level_copies n 1 (ih (hf 1))))
      (localize_level_copies n 2 (ih (hf 2)))) (localize_level_copies n 3 (ih (hf 3))))
      (localize_level_copies n 4 (ih (hf 4)))


private def FinitaryAt (n : ℕ) (g : Γ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (v : W), n ≤ v.length → ∀ w : W, g.1 (v ++ w) = g.1 v ++ w

private def finitary : Subgroup Γ where
  carrier := {g | ∃ n, FinitaryAt n g}
  one_mem' := ⟨0, fun _ _ _ => rfl⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro g h ⟨n, hg⟩ ⟨m, hh⟩
    refine ⟨max n m, fun v hv w => ?_⟩
    change g.1 (h.1 (v ++ w)) = g.1 (h.1 v) ++ w
    rw [hh v ((le_max_right n m).trans hv) w]
    exact hg (h.1 v) (by simpa using (le_max_left n m).trans hv) w
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro g ⟨n, hg⟩
    refine ⟨n, fun v hv w => g.1.injective ?_⟩
    change g.1 (g.1.symm (v ++ w)) = g.1 (g.1.symm v ++ w)
    rw [hg _ (by simpa only [← show (g⁻¹ : Γ).1 = g.1.symm from rfl, act_length] using hv)]
    simp

private theorem directed_replicate (a : A) (n : ℕ) (w : W) :
    directed a (List.replicate n 0 ++ w) = List.replicate n 0 ++ directed a w := by
  induction n with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih => simp [List.replicate_succ, ih]

private theorem finitary_ne_top : finitary ≠ ⊤ := by
  intro h
  have ht : directedG turn ∈ finitary := h ▸ Subgroup.mem_top _
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := ht
  have hw := hn (List.replicate n 0) (by simp) [1, 0]
  change directed turn (List.replicate n 0 ++ [1, 0]) =
    directed turn (List.replicate n 0) ++ [1, 0] at hw
  have hrep : directed turn (List.replicate n 0) = List.replicate n 0 := by
    simpa using directed_replicate turn n []
  rw [directed_replicate, hrep] at hw
  have hfix := List.append_cancel_left hw
  simp [turn_zero] at hfix

private theorem finitary_approx (n : ℕ) (g : Γ) :
    ∃ h : Γ, FinitaryAt n h ∧ ∀ v : Level n, h.1 v.1 = g.1 v.1 := by
  induction n generalizing g with
  | zero =>
    refine ⟨1, fun _ _ _ => rfl, fun ⟨v, hv⟩ => ?_⟩
    simp [List.length_eq_zero_iff.mp hv]
  | succ n ih =>
    obtain ⟨a, f, rfl⟩ := assemble_decompose g
    choose h hfinite hagree using fun x : X => ih (f x)
    refine ⟨assemble a h, ?_, ?_⟩
    · intro v hv w
      cases v with
      | nil => simp at hv
      | cons x v =>
        simp only [List.cons_append, assemble_cons, List.cons.injEq, true_and]
        exact hfinite x v (Nat.le_of_succ_le_succ hv) w
    · rintro ⟨(_ | ⟨x, v⟩), hv⟩
      · simp at hv
      · simp only [assemble_cons, List.cons.injEq, true_and]
        exact hagree x ⟨v, Nat.succ.inj hv⟩

private theorem generators_sup : rootG.range ⊔ directedG.range = (⊤ : Subgroup Γ) := by
  apply Subgroup.map_injective exampleGroup.subtype_injective
  rw [Subgroup.map_sup, ← MonoidHom.range_comp, ← MonoidHom.range_comp,
    Subgroup.map_top, Subgroup.range_subtype]
  rfl

private instance examplePerfect : Group.IsPerfect Γ := by
  rw [Group.isPerfect_def, eq_top_iff, ← generators_sup]
  have h (f : A →* Γ) : f.range ≤ commutator Γ := by
    have := Group.IsPerfect.range f
    rw [← Subgroup.commutator_eq_self (H := f.range)]
    exact Subgroup.commutator_mono le_top le_top
  exact sup_le (h rootG) (h directedG)

private theorem local_g_commute {x y : X} (hxy : x ≠ y) (g h : Γ) :
    Commute (localG x g) (localG y h) := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨z, w⟩)
  · rfl
  · change localize x g.1 (localize y h.1 (z :: w)) =
      localize y h.1 (localize x g.1 (z :: w))
    by_cases hx : x = z
    · subst z
      simp [Ne.symm hxy]
    · by_cases hy : y = z
      · subst z
        simp [hxy]
      · simp [hx, hy]

-- These copies are supported on pairwise disjoint subtrees, at the words 0ⁿ1.
private def sideCopy (n : ℕ) : Γ →* Γ := embed (List.replicate n 0 ++ [1])

private theorem side_commute (n m : ℕ) (hnm : n ≠ m) (g h : Γ) :
    Commute (sideCopy n g) (sideCopy m h) := by
  induction n generalizing m with
  | zero =>
    cases m with
    | zero => exact (hnm rfl).elim
    | succ m => exact local_g_commute (by decide) g (sideCopy m h)
  | succ n ih =>
    cases m with
    | zero => exact local_g_commute (by decide) (sideCopy n g) h
    | succ m =>
      exact (ih m (fun h => hnm (congrArg Nat.succ h))).map (localG 0)

private theorem embed_conjugate (v w : W) (hl : v.length = w.length) :
    ∃ k : Γ, ∀ g : Γ, k * embed v g * k⁻¹ = embed w g := by
  induction v generalizing w with
  | nil =>
    have : w = [] := List.length_eq_zero_iff.mp hl.symm
    subst w
    exact ⟨1, fun g => by simp⟩
  | cons x v ih =>
    cases w with
    | nil => simp at hl
    | cons y w =>
      obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := ih w (Nat.succ.inj hl)
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := letter_transitive x y
      refine ⟨rootG a * localG x k, fun g => ?_⟩
      calc
        _ = rootG a * localG x (k * embed v g * k⁻¹) * (rootG a)⁻¹ := by
          simp only [embed_cons, map_mul, map_inv]
          group
        _ = rootG a * localG x (embed w g) * (rootG a)⁻¹ := by rw [hk]
        _ = embed (y :: w) g := Subtype.ext (by
          change root a * localize x (embed w g).1 * (root a)⁻¹ = localize y (embed w g).1
          rw [root_conj_localize, ha])

-- Equal images of two commuting perfect copies are trivial. Conjugating then kills
-- every copy at the depth of the first one.
private theorem kills_level_copies {Q : Type*} [Group Q] [Finite Q] (φ : Γ →* Q) :
    ∃ n, levelCopies n ≤ φ.ker := by
  let J (n : ℕ) : Subgroup Q := (φ.comp (sideCopy n)).range
  have : Finite (Subgroup Q) := Finite.of_injective (fun H : Subgroup Q => (H : Set Q))
    SetLike.coe_injective
  obtain ⟨i, j, hij, heq⟩ := Finite.exists_ne_map_eq_of_infinite J
  have hcomm : ⁅J i, J i⁆ ≤ ⊥ := by
    apply Subgroup.commutator_le.mpr
    intro a ha b hb
    have hb' : b ∈ J j := heq ▸ hb
    obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := ha
    obtain ⟨h, rfl⟩ := hb'
    exact Subgroup.mem_bot.mpr ((side_commute i j hij g h).map φ).commutator_eq
  have : Group.IsPerfect (J i) := Group.IsPerfect.range _
  rw [Subgroup.commutator_eq_self] at hcomm
  have hkill (g : Γ) : φ (sideCopy i g) = 1 :=
    Subgroup.mem_bot.mp (hcomm (show φ (sideCopy i g) ∈ J i from ⟨g, rfl⟩))
  refine ⟨i + 1, iSup_le fun v => ?_⟩
  rintro _ ⟨g, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := embed_conjugate (List.replicate i 0 ++ [1]) v.1 (by simp [v.2])
  apply MonoidHom.mem_ker.mpr
  rw [← hk, map_mul, map_mul, show φ (embed (List.replicate i 0 ++ [1]) g) = 1 from hkill g,
    mul_one, map_inv, mul_inv_cancel]

private theorem finitary_hits_finite {Q : Type*} [Group Q] [Finite Q] (φ : Γ →* Q) (g : Γ) :
    ∃ h ∈ finitary, φ h = φ g := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := kills_level_copies φ
  obtain ⟨h, hf, ha⟩ := finitary_approx n g
  refine ⟨h, ⟨n, hf⟩, ?_⟩
  have he : levelAction n h = levelAction n g :=
    Equiv.ext fun w => Subtype.ext (ha w)
  have hm : h * g⁻¹ ∈ (levelAction n).ker := by
    simp [MonoidHom.mem_ker, he]
  have hφ := MonoidHom.mem_ker.mp (hn (level_ker_le_copies n hm))
  rwa [map_mul, map_inv, mul_inv_eq_one] at hφ


private theorem top_compact : IsCompactElement (⊤ : Subgroup Γ) := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := Subgroup.isMulFG_iff.mp (Group.fg_def.mp exampleFG)
  apply (isCompactElement_iff_le_of_directed_sSup_le _).mpr
  intro c hc hd htop
  have hsub : (S : Set Γ) ⊆ ⋃ K ∈ c, (K : Set Γ) := by
    intro g hg
    have hg' : g ∈ sSup c := htop (Subgroup.mem_top g)
    obtain ⟨K, hK, hgK⟩ := (Subgroup.mem_sSup_of_directedOn hc hd).mp hg'
    exact Set.mem_iUnion₂.mpr ⟨K, hK, hgK⟩
  obtain ⟨K, hK, hSK⟩ := hd.exists_mem_subset_of_finset_subset_biUnion hc hsub
  exact ⟨K, hK, hS ▸ (Subgroup.closure_le (K := K)).2 hSK⟩

private theorem exists_infinite_index_coatom : ∃ M : Subgroup Γ, IsCoatom M ∧ ¬ M.FiniteIndex := by
  have := CompleteLattice.coatomic_of_top_compact top_compact
  obtain ⟨M, hM, hFM⟩ := (eq_top_or_exists_le_coatom finitary).resolve_left finitary_ne_top
  refine ⟨M, hM, fun hfin => hM.ne_top ?_⟩
  apply top_unique
  intro g _
  let φ : Γ →* Γ ⧸ M.normalCore := QuotientGroup.mk' M.normalCore
  obtain ⟨h, hh, he⟩ := finitary_hits_finite φ g
  have hk : h⁻¹ * g ∈ M.normalCore := by
    apply (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).mp
    change φ (h⁻¹ * g) = 1
    simp [he]
  have hg := M.mul_mem (hFM hh) (M.normalCore_le hk)
  simpa using hg

private def wordEquiv : W ≃ TreeVertex (fun _ => 5) where
  toFun w :=
    ⟨w.map Fin.val, fun i hi => by
      rw [List.getElem_map]
      exact Fin.isLt _⟩
  invFun v := List.ofFn fun i : Fin v.1.length => (⟨v.1[i], v.2 i.1 i.2⟩ : X)
  left_inv w := by
    apply List.ext_getElem (by simp)
    intro i hi _
    apply Fin.ext
    simp
  right_inv v := by
    apply Subtype.ext
    apply List.ext_getElem (by simp)
    intro i hi _
    simp

private theorem word_prefix (v w : W) :
    (wordEquiv v).1 <+: (wordEquiv w).1 ↔ v <+: w := by
  change v.map Fin.val <+: w.map Fin.val ↔ _
  induction v generalizing w with
  | nil => simp
  | cons x v ih =>
    cases w with
    | nil => simp
    | cons y w => simp [List.cons_prefix_cons, ih, Fin.val_inj]

private def treeAction : Γ →* Equiv.Perm (TreeVertex (fun _ => 5)) :=
  wordEquiv.permCongrHom.toMonoidHom.comp exampleGroup.subtype

@[simp] private theorem tree_action_word (g : Γ) (w : W) :
    treeAction g (wordEquiv w) = wordEquiv (g.1 w) := by
  change wordEquiv (g.1 (wordEquiv.symm (wordEquiv w))) = _
  rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]

private theorem example_branch : IsBranchGroup Γ := by
  refine ⟨fun _ => 5, fun _ => (by decide : 2 ≤ 5), treeAction,
    wordEquiv.permCongrHom.injective.comp exampleGroup.subtype_injective, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro g v w
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := wordEquiv.surjective v
    obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := wordEquiv.surjective w
    simpa only [tree_action_word, word_prefix] using act_prefix g v w
  · intro v w h
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := wordEquiv.surjective v
    obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := wordEquiv.surjective w
    change (v.map Fin.val).length = (w.map Fin.val).length at h
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := level_transitive v w (by simpa only [List.length_map] using h)
    exact ⟨g, by simp [hg]⟩
  · intro n
    apply Subgroup.finiteIndex_of_le (H := (levelAction n).ker)
    apply (level_ker_le_copies n).trans
    apply iSup_le
    rintro v _ ⟨g, rfl⟩
    apply Subgroup.subset_closure
    apply Set.mem_iUnion₂.mpr
    refine ⟨wordEquiv v.1, ?_, ?_⟩
    · change (v.1.map Fin.val).length = n
      simpa only [List.length_map] using v.2
    · intro w hw
      obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := wordEquiv.surjective w
      rw [word_prefix] at hw
      rw [tree_action_word, embed_fixes _ _ _ hw]

/--
**A finitely generated branch group with a maximal subgroup of infinite index.** The
Kourovka 15.15 statement that every maximal subgroup of a finitely generated branch group has
finite index is false: some finitely generated branch group has a maximal subgroup of infinite
index.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D.
Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 15.15 (L. Bartholdi, R. I.
Grigorchuk, Z. Šunić); resolution: I. V. Bondarenko, Finite generation of iterated wreath products,
Arch. Math. (Basel) 95 (2010), no. 4, 301-308, arXiv:1002.0320, abstract and the example after
Corollary 3 (a finitely generated branch group with maximal subgroups of infinite index, answering
Question 14 of Bartholdi, Grigorchuk and Šunić, Branch groups); Kourovka Archive, Problem 15.15
(answer: No, not necessarily), https://arxiv.org/abs/1002.0320.
-/
public theorem branchGroupMaximalSubgroupsFiniteIndex_refuted :
    ¬ branchGroupMaximalSubgroupsFiniteIndex := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨M, hM, hInfinite⟩ := exists_infinite_index_coatom
  exact hInfinite (h Γ exampleFG example_branch M hM)

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.BranchGroupInfiniteIndexMaximalKourovka15Problem15Wanted
